cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RAGProbe: canary-scored prompt-injection testing for LLM, RAG and agent applications"
message: "If you use RAGProbe or its benchmark, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Jain"
    given-names: "Khushi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/khushi-git-7/ragprobe"
url: "https://khushi-git-7.github.io/ragprobe/"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - prompt-injection
  - llm-security
  - red-teaming
  - rag
  - benchmark
  - evaluation
  - owasp
abstract: >-
  RAGProbe tests LLM, RAG and agent applications against the OWASP Top 10 for
  LLM Applications and scores the result with planted canaries instead of a
  judge model. Each attack asks for two random marker halves to be emitted
  joined, while the attack text contains them only separately, so a joined
  marker is evidence that the application followed an instruction arriving in
  the message body and scoring reduces to a string comparison. Leak attacks
  plant a secret and check the reply reversed, rot13, base64 and hex encoded.
  The bundled benchmark is frozen and versioned: v2 contains all of v1 with the
  same item ids and splits, splits are assigned by hashing item ids, detectors
  are tuned on a development split and reported on a held-out test split, and
  every run writes a manifest and a cached transcript so published numbers can
  be re-scored without API access. The harness reports paired significance
  tests and confidence intervals, and every defence also reports the ordinary
  requests it wrongly blocks.
references:
  - type: data
    title: "RAGProbe Bench v2"
    url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/Khushi-7/ragprobe-bench"
